# Object params

Convention (no backing skill). Functions/methods with **2+ parameters** take a single named options object, **except** repository files, constructors (dependency injection, wired once in the containers) and framework callbacks — the exact Fastify shapes `(request, reply)`, `(request, reply, done)`, `(error, request, reply)`, and array callbacks. A helper of ours that takes `request` or `reply` plus anything else is not a framework callback and takes an options object. Reduces arg-order bugs, keeps call sites self-documenting and signatures stable. A signature a library calls positionally (BullMQ backoff strategies, `@fastify/rate-limit`'s store and `onExceeded`, Fastify hooks registered by reference, an ioredis Lua command) keeps its shape and is listed in the test's `FRAMEWORK_DICTATED` allowlist. **Enforced** for every non-test, non-repository file under `src/` by `src/tests/global/object-params.global.test.ts`. Detail: CLAUDE.md › Naming Conventions.
